# shield/arm: the shield arm (P2c slice, SLICE-HELM-SHIELD): the off (left) arm of every shield bearer (`role shield arm`),
# on its own channel `sharm` (a shield bearer's clips name armL=- sharm=<key>; P2C_CONTRACTS 4). It carries the shield:
# every view marks gripL (the fist on the shield's grip), which places the shield (shield/kite and the other shapes).
# Regions U F C H as the arm library's, so the sleeve, the bracer, mail, plate and gloves recolour it (regionsOf). It does
# not swing: at rest and in the walk the shield hangs still on the arm (STYLE_P2 25.5); the run hugs it to the body; guard
# raises it to the chest; block squares it to the threat; hurt drops it a pixel; fling is the fall's recoil; lie the
# corpse's arm. Swing keys: shtuck (the shield tucked in while the sword arm swings: the guard's windup, strike and
# follow) and guard (his recover). Facing right it is the far arm (behind the body), so its views there are the grip
# marks and a knuckle. Shared by both bodies (the shoulders and the arm library match). Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
use person
body adult
role shield arm
layer armNear
anchor shoulderL
keys sharm
side L

view D key rest origin 1 -1
mark gripL 1 6
|765
|765
|765
|765
|hgf
|hgf
|tsq
|srq
|qq.
regions
|UUU
|UUU
|FFF
|FFF
|CCC
